IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-sch2-forces`

-- PART 4 -- RESIDENCE AND PRESENCE CONDITIONS, first half: regulations 16 to 21.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Regulation 16 sets four conditions, each tested on a day for which C claims
-- personal independence payment; regulations 17 to 21 treat C as present, or as habitually resident, or
-- disapply a limb. The rest of Part 4 (22 to 23A) and the combination of everything into one answer are in
-- pip-part4-special-cases.l4.
--
-- Each limb is a rule of its own, taking as inputs the ways the later regulations modify it, so that no
-- rule here depends on a rule of the other module.

§ `Regulation 16: the four conditions`

DECLARE `a place of habitual residence` IS ONE OF
    `the United Kingdom`
    `the Republic of Ireland`
    `the Isle of Man`
    `the Channel Islands`
    `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland`
    `Switzerland`
    `some other place`

-- reg 16(a): C is present in England and Wales (on the day).
-- C is treated as present by regulations 17 to 19 (absence), 20A (absence while present in Scotland), and
-- 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7) (the run-on period after a move to Scotland); regulation 23ZC(6) reads "England and
-- Wales" as "Great Britain" for the decision on an ongoing claim. Out of text: the place C is present is a fact.
-- src:171 | Subject to the following provisions of this Part, the prescribed conditions for the purposes of section 77(3) of the Act as to residence and presence in Great Britain are that on any day for which C claims personal independence payment C—
-- src:172 | (a) is present in England and Wales;
@ref reg 16(a) (src:171-172)
GIVEN `C is present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is present in Great Britain on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 16(a) is read with "Great Britain" in place of "England and Wales"` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(a): C is present in England and Wales on the day` MEANS
    IF `regulation 16(a) is read with "Great Britain" in place of "England and Wales"`
    THEN `C is present in Great Britain on the day` OR `C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day`
    ELSE `C is present in England and Wales on the day` OR `C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day`

-- reg 16(b): C has been present in Great Britain for a period of, or periods amounting in aggregate to, not less
-- than 104 weeks out of the 156 weeks immediately preceding that day. The weeks C was treated as present
-- (regulations 17 to 19) count as weeks of presence ("treated as present ... for the purposes of regulation
-- 16(a) and (b)").
-- src:173 | (b) has been present in Great Britain for a period of, or periods amounting in aggregate to, not less than 104 weeks out of the 156 weeks immediately preceding that day;
@ref reg 16(b) (src:173)
`reg 16(b): the weeks of presence in Great Britain required` MEANS 104

@ref reg 16(b) (src:173)
GIVEN `the weeks C was present in Great Britain out of the 156 weeks immediately preceding the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks C was treated as present in Great Britain out of those 156 weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(b): C has been present in Great Britain for not less than 104 weeks out of the 156 weeks` MEANS
    (`the weeks C was present in Great Britain out of the 156 weeks immediately preceding the day` PLUS `the weeks C was treated as present in Great Britain out of those 156 weeks`)
        AT LEAST `reg 16(b): the weeks of presence in Great Britain required`

-- reg 16(c): C is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Republic of Ireland, the Isle of Man or the Channel Islands.
-- src:174 | (c) is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Republic of Ireland, the Isle of Man or the Channel Islands; and
@ref reg 16(c) (src:174)
GIVEN place IS A `a place of habitual residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(c): C is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Republic of Ireland, the Isle of Man or the Channel Islands` place MEANS
       place EQUALS `the United Kingdom`
    OR place EQUALS `the Republic of Ireland`
    OR place EQUALS `the Isle of Man`
    OR place EQUALS `the Channel Islands`

-- reg 16(d): C is a person (i) who is not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the
-- Immigration and Asylum Act 1999; or (ii) to whom, by virtue of regulation 2 of the Social Security (Immigration
-- and Asylum) Consequential Amendments Regulations 2000, section 115 of that Act does not apply for the purpose
-- of personal independence payment.
-- out of text: Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 s 115(9); Social Security (Immigration and Asylum) Consequential Amendments Regulations 2000 reg 2
-- src:175 | (d) is a person–
-- src:176 | (i) who is not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 ; or
-- src:177 | (ii) to whom, by virtue of regulation 2 of the Social Security (Immigration and Asylum) Consequential Amendments Regulations 2000 , section 115 of that Act does not apply for the purpose of personal independence payment.
@ref reg 16(d) (src:175-177)
GIVEN `C is not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 115 of that Act does not apply to C for the purpose of personal independence payment by virtue of regulation 2 of the 2000 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(d): C is a person who is not excluded by immigration control` MEANS
       `C is not subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999`
    OR `section 115 of that Act does not apply to C for the purpose of personal independence payment by virtue of regulation 2 of the 2000 Regulations`

§ `Regulation 16A: the relevant area`

DECLARE `a limb of regulation 16 that names a relevant area` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 16(a)`
    `regulation 16(b)`

DECLARE `a relevant area` IS ONE OF
    `England and Wales`
    `Great Britain`

-- src:178 | 16A Meaning of “the relevant area” in this Part
-- src:179 | In this Part, “the relevant area” means—
-- src:180 | (a) for the purposes of regulation 16(a), England and Wales;
-- src:181 | (b) for the purposes of regulation 16(b), Great Britain.
@ref reg 16A (src:178-181)
GIVEN limb IS A `a limb of regulation 16 that names a relevant area`
GIVETH A `a relevant area`
`reg 16A: the relevant area for the limb` limb MEANS
    CONSIDER limb
    WHEN `regulation 16(a)` THEN `England and Wales`
    WHEN `regulation 16(b)` THEN `Great Britain`

§ `Regulations 17 to 18D: absence from Great Britain`

-- The facts about one absence from Great Britain that regulations 17 to 19 turn on. The seat asks for them in
-- the person's own words; regulation 19(1) is worked out by its own rule below and enters as one fact.
DECLARE `an absence from Great Britain` HAS
    `at the beginning of the absence, the absence was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the absence is solely in connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which commenced before C left Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period whilst C is temporarily absent from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the treatment is by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or have returned, to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation 19(1) applies to the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the weeks of the absence that fall within the 156 weeks` IS A NUMBER

-- reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent if, at the beginning of the period of absence, C's absence is unlikely to exceed 52 weeks.
-- Regulations 18(2), 18A(2) and 18C(2) give "temporarily absent" the same meaning.
-- src:184 | (2) C is temporarily absent if, at the beginning of the period of absence, C's absence is unlikely to exceed 52 weeks.
@ref reg 17(2) (src:184)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent` a MEANS
    a's `at the beginning of the absence, the absence was unlikely to exceed 52 weeks`

-- reg 17(1): where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the
-- purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) for the first 13 weeks of absence. The rule gives the number of weeks
-- from the start of the absence for which C is treated as present by this regulation: 13, or none.
-- src:183 | (1) Where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) for the first 13 weeks of absence.
@ref reg 17(1) (src:183)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 17(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a MEANS
    IF `reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent` a THEN 13 ELSE 0

-- reg 18(1): where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the
-- purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) for the first 26 weeks of that absence, where (a) C's absence is solely in
-- connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement
-- which commenced before C left Great Britain; and (b) the arrangements relate to medical treatment (i) outside
-- Great Britain; (ii) during the period whilst C is temporarily absent; and (iii) by, or under the supervision of, a
-- person appropriately qualified to carry out that treatment.
-- src:185 | 18 Absence from Great Britain to receive medical treatment
-- src:186 | (1) Where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) for the first 26 weeks of that absence, where—
-- src:187 | (a) C's absence is solely in connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which commenced before C left Great Britain; and
-- src:188 | (b) the arrangements referred to in paragraph (1)(a) relate to medical treatment –
-- src:189 | (i) outside Great Britain;
-- src:190 | (ii) during the period whilst C is temporarily absent from Great Britain; and
-- src:191 | (iii) by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry out that treatment.
-- src:192 | (2) In this regulation, “temporarily absent” has the same meaning as in regulation 17(2).
@ref reg 18(1), reg 18(2) (src:186-192)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a MEANS
    IF     `reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent` a
       AND a's `the absence is solely in connection with arrangements made for the medical treatment of C for a disease or bodily or mental disablement which commenced before C left Great Britain`
       AND a's `the arrangements relate to medical treatment outside Great Britain`
       AND a's `the arrangements relate to medical treatment during the period whilst C is temporarily absent from Great Britain`
       AND a's `the treatment is by, or under the supervision of, a person appropriately qualified to carry it out`
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- reg 18A(1): where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the
-- purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) during the first 26 weeks of that absence, where (a) C was present in a
-- country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government (i) provided public
-- information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or (ii) arranged the evacuation of
-- British nationals from it; (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to
-- return, or have returned, to Great Britain; and (c) C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's
-- Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it.
-- The converter shows "{repealed: Great Britain}" beside "the relevant area"; the words are read as struck.
-- src:193 | 18A Absence where His Majesty’s Government provides public information to advise British nationals to leave a country or territory or arranges the evacuation of British nationals from a country or territory
-- src:194 | (1) Where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in {repealed: Great Britain} the relevant area for the purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) during the first 26 weeks of that absence, where—
-- src:195 | (a) C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:196 | (i) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:197 | (ii) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory;
-- src:198 | (b) the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or have returned, to Great Britain; and
-- src:199 | (c) C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty’s Government’s public information was to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory.
-- src:200 | (2) In this regulation, “temporarily absent” has the same meaning as in regulation 17(2).
@ref reg 18A(1), reg 18A(2) (src:194-200)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18A(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a MEANS
    IF     `reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent` a
       AND `reg 18A(1)(a): C was present in the country or territory immediately before the Government's advice or evacuation` a
       AND a's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or have returned, to Great Britain`
       AND a's `C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it`
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

@ref reg 18A(1)(a) (src:195-197)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18A(1)(a): C was present in the country or territory immediately before the Government's advice or evacuation` a MEANS
       a's `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it`
    OR a's `C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it`

-- reg 18C(1): the same as regulation 18A(1) with "the Scottish Ministers" as the person who must be satisfied (b). The
-- text has both versions (fork F-21): C may be treated as present by either.
-- src:203 | 18C Absence where His Majesty’s Government provides public information to advise British nationals to leave a country or territory or arranges the evacuation of British nationals from a country or territory
-- src:204 | (1) Where C is temporarily absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b) during the first 26 weeks of that absence, where—
-- src:205 | (a) C was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:206 | (i) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:207 | (ii) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory,
-- src:208 | (b) the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain, and
-- src:209 | (c) C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty’s Government’s public information was to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory.
-- src:210 | (2) In this regulation, “temporarily absent” has the same meaning as in regulation 17(2).
@ref reg 18C(1), reg 18C(2) (src:204-210)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18C(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a MEANS
    IF     `reg 17(2): C is temporarily absent` a
       AND `reg 18A(1)(a): C was present in the country or territory immediately before the Government's advice or evacuation` a
       AND a's `the Scottish Ministers are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect C to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain`
       AND a's `C did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it`
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- Two numbers: the larger, the smaller. (The prelude's own names are avoided.)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers` x y MEANS
    IF x AT LEAST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regs 17 to 18D: the smaller of two numbers` x y MEANS
    IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

-- reg 18B: where a person is temporarily absent from Great Britain in the circumstances specified in regulation 17(1),
-- 18(1) or 18A(1), the total period of an absence where C is treated as present in the relevant area will not
-- exceed 26 weeks. The three periods all run from the start of the absence, so the total is the longest of them,
-- and not more than 26 weeks.
-- src:201 | 18B Time limits on absences where the claimant is treated as being in Great Britain
-- src:202 | Where a person is temporarily absent from Great Britain in the circumstances specified in regulation 17(1), 18(1) or 18A(1), the total period of an absence where C is treated as present in {repealed: Great Britain} the relevant area will not exceed 26 weeks.
@ref reg 18B (src:201-202)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18B: the total weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present under regulations 17(1), 18(1) and 18A(1)` a MEANS
    `regs 17 to 18D: the smaller of two numbers` 26
        (`regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers` (`reg 17(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)
            (`regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers` (`reg 18(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)
                (`reg 18A(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)))

-- reg 18D(1): the same limit for regulations 17(1), 18(1) and 18C(1).
-- src:211 | 18D Time limits on absences where the claimant is treated as being in Great Britain
-- src:212 | (1) Where a person is temporarily absent from Great Britain in the circumstances specified in regulation 17(1), 18(1) or 18C(1), the total period of an absence where C is treated as present in the relevant area will not exceed 26 weeks.
@ref reg 18D(1) (src:211-212)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 18D(1): the total weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present under regulations 17(1), 18(1) and 18C(1)` a MEANS
    `regs 17 to 18D: the smaller of two numbers` 26
        (`regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers` (`reg 17(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)
            (`regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers` (`reg 18(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)
                (`reg 18C(1): the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)))

-- Both limits together: the weeks from the start of the absence for which C is treated as present under regulations 17 to 18D.
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regs 17 to 18D: the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a MEANS
    `regs 17 to 18D: the larger of two numbers`
        (`reg 18B: the total weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present under regulations 17(1), 18(1) and 18A(1)` a)
        (`reg 18D(1): the total weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present under regulations 17(1), 18(1) and 18C(1)` a)

§ `Regulation 19: absence in special cases`

-- reg 19(2): "a member of Her Majesty's forces" means a member of "the regular forces" or "the reserve forces" as defined
-- in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006, other than a person who is specified in Schedule 2, who is (a) over the
-- age of 16; and (b) not absent on desertion. "Over the age of 16" is read strictly: C is over 16 on any day after the
-- 16th birthday, and not on the birthday itself (fork F-19).
-- out of text: Armed Forces Act 2006 s 374
-- src:221 | (2) In this regulation and in regulation 20, “a member of Her Majesty's forces” means a member of “the regular forces” or “the reserve forces” as defined in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006 , other than a person who is specified in Schedule 2, who is–
-- src:222 | (a) over the age of 16; and
-- src:223 | (b) not absent on desertion.
@ref reg 19(2) (src:221-223)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the regular forces or the reserve forces as defined in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is specified in Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the person is absent on desertion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(2): the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces on the day` MEANS
        `the person is a member of the regular forces or the reserve forces as defined in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006`
    AND (NOT `the person is specified in Schedule 2`)
    AND (`add years` `the person's date of birth` 16) LESS THAN `the day`
    AND (NOT `the person is absent on desertion`)

-- reg 19(3), "aircraft worker": a person who is employed under a contract of service either as a pilot, commander,
-- navigator or other member of the crew of any aircraft, or in any other capacity on board any aircraft where (a) the
-- employment in that other capacity is for the purposes of the aircraft or its crew or of any passengers or cargo or
-- mail carried on that aircraft; and (b) the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its
-- performance (in whole or in part) while the aircraft is in flight, but does not include a person who is in employment
-- as a member of Her Majesty's forces. The "where" is read as qualifying the second alternative, "any other
-- capacity" (fork F-20).
-- src:224 | (3) In this regulation—
-- src:225 | “aircraft worker” means a person who is employed under a contract of service either as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of any aircraft, or in any other capacity on board any aircraft where–
-- src:226 | (a) the employment in that other capacity is for the purposes of the aircraft or its crew or of any passengers or cargo or mail carried on that aircraft; and
-- src:227 | (b) the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance (in whole or in part) while the aircraft is in flight,
-- src:228 | but does not include a person who is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces;
@ref reg 19(3) "aircraft worker" (src:224-228)
GIVEN `the person is in employment on board an aircraft in another capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that employment is for the purposes of the aircraft or its crew or of any passengers or cargo or mail carried on the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance in whole or in part while the aircraft is in flight` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) "aircraft worker": the other-capacity limb is met` MEANS
        `the person is in employment on board an aircraft in another capacity`
    AND `that employment is for the purposes of the aircraft or its crew or of any passengers or cargo or mail carried on the aircraft`
    AND `the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance in whole or in part while the aircraft is in flight`

@ref reg 19(3) "aircraft worker" (src:225-228)
GIVEN `the person is employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other-capacity limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3): the person is an aircraft worker` MEANS
        `the person is employed under a contract of service`
    AND (NOT `the person is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces`)
    AND `reg 19(3) "aircraft worker": the crew limb or the other-capacity limb` `the person is employed as a pilot, commander, navigator or other member of the crew of an aircraft` `the other-capacity limb is met`

GIVEN `the person is employed as a crew member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other-capacity limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) "aircraft worker": the crew limb or the other-capacity limb` `the person is employed as a crew member` `the other-capacity limb is met` MEANS
    `the person is employed as a crew member` OR `the other-capacity limb is met`

-- reg 19(3), "mariner": the same for a ship or vessel: employed under a contract of service either as a master or member
-- of the crew of any ship or vessel, or in any other capacity on board any ship or vessel where (a) the employment in
-- that other capacity is for the purposes of that ship or vessel or the crew or any passengers or cargo or mail carried by
-- it; and (b) the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance (in whole or in part)
-- while the ship or vessel is on voyage, but does not include a person who is in employment as a member of Her
-- Majesty's forces.
-- src:229 | “mariner” means a person who is in employment under a contract of service either as a master or member of the crew of any ship or vessel, or in any other capacity on board any ship or vessel where –
-- src:230 | (a) the employment in that other capacity is for the purposes of that ship or vessel or the crew or any passengers or cargo or mail carried by the ship or vessel; and
-- src:231 | (b) the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance (in whole or in part) while the ship or vessel is on voyage,
-- src:232 | but does not include a person who is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces.
@ref reg 19(3) "mariner" (src:229-232)
GIVEN `the person is in employment on board a ship or vessel in another capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that employment is for the purposes of the ship or vessel or the crew or any passengers or cargo or mail carried by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance in whole or in part while the ship or vessel is on voyage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) "mariner": the other-capacity limb is met` MEANS
        `the person is in employment on board a ship or vessel in another capacity`
    AND `that employment is for the purposes of the ship or vessel or the crew or any passengers or cargo or mail carried by it`
    AND `the contract is entered into in the United Kingdom with a view to its performance in whole or in part while the ship or vessel is on voyage`

@ref reg 19(3) "mariner" (src:229-232)
GIVEN `the person is employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed as a master or member of the crew of a ship or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other-capacity limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3): the person is a mariner` MEANS
        `the person is employed under a contract of service`
    AND (NOT `the person is in employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces`)
    AND `reg 19(3) "mariner": the crew limb or the other-capacity limb` `the person is employed as a master or member of the crew of a ship or vessel` `the other-capacity limb is met`

GIVEN `the person is employed as a master or crew member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other-capacity limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) "mariner": the crew limb or the other-capacity limb` `the person is employed as a master or crew member` `the other-capacity limb is met` MEANS
    `the person is employed as a master or crew member` OR `the other-capacity limb is met`

-- The relations to a member of Her Majesty's forces that regulations 19(1)(c) and 20(b) list: spouse, civil partner,
-- son, daughter, step-son, step-daughter, father, father-in-law, step-father, mother, mother-in-law or step-mother.
DECLARE `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `civil partner`
    `son`
    `daughter`
    `step-son`
    `step-daughter`
    `father`
    `father-in-law`
    `step-father`
    `mother`
    `mother-in-law`
    `step-mother`
    `some other relationship`

@ref reg 19(1)(c), reg 20(b) (src:220, src:236)
GIVEN r IS A `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 19(1)(c) and 20(b): the relationship is one that the regulation lists` r MEANS
    NOT (r EQUALS `some other relationship`)

-- reg 19(1): where C is absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the purposes of
-- regulation 16(a) and (b), where (a) C is abroad in the capacity of (i) a member of Her Majesty's forces; (ii) an aircraft
-- worker; or (iii) a mariner; or (b) C is in employment prescribed for the purposes of section 120 (employment at sea
-- (continental shelf operations)) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 in connection with continental
-- shelf operations; or (c) C is living with a person mentioned in paragraph (a)(i) and is the spouse, civil partner, son,
-- daughter, step-son, step-daughter, father, father-in-law, step-father, mother, mother-in-law or step-mother of that person.
-- out of text: Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 s 120 and the regulations prescribing the employment
-- src:213 | 19 Absence from Great Britain in special cases
-- src:214 | (1) Where C is absent from Great Britain, C is treated as present in the relevant area for the purposes of regulation 16(a) and (b), where —
-- src:215 | (a) C is abroad in the capacity of–
-- src:216 | (i) a member of Her Majesty's forces;
-- src:217 | (ii) an aircraft worker; or
-- src:218 | (iii) a mariner; or
-- src:219 | (b) C is in employment prescribed for the purposes of section 120 (employment at sea (continental shelf operations)) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 in connection with continental shelf operations; or
-- src:220 | (c) C is living with a person mentioned in paragraph (a)(i) and is the spouse, civil partner, son, daughter, step-son, step-daughter, father, father-in-law, step-father, mother, mother-in-law or step-mother of that person.
@ref reg 19(1) (src:214-220)
GIVEN `C is abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is abroad in the capacity of an aircraft worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is abroad in the capacity of a mariner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is in employment prescribed for the purposes of section 120 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is living with a person who is abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's relationship to that person` IS A `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(1): one of the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (c) applies` MEANS
       `C is abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces`
    OR `C is abroad in the capacity of an aircraft worker`
    OR `C is abroad in the capacity of a mariner`
    OR `C is in employment prescribed for the purposes of section 120 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 in connection with continental shelf operations`
    OR (    `C is living with a person who is abroad in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces`
        AND `regs 19(1)(c) and 20(b): the relationship is one that the regulation lists` `C's relationship to that person`)

@ref reg 19(1) (src:214)
GIVEN `C is absent from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (c) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19(1): C is treated as present in the relevant area` `C is absent from Great Britain` `one of the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (c) applies` MEANS
    `C is absent from Great Britain` AND `one of the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (c) applies`

§ `Regulations 17 to 19 applied to a day and to the 156 weeks`

-- For regulation 16(a): C is treated as present in the relevant area on a day of an absence if regulation 19(1)
-- applies to the absence, or the day falls within the first weeks of the absence for which regulations 17 to 18D
-- treat C as present. A day is "within the first N weeks" when the weeks of absence as at that day do not exceed N.
@ref reg 17(1), reg 18(1), reg 18A(1), reg 18C(1), reg 19(1) (src:183, src:186, src:194, src:204, src:214)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
      `the weeks of the absence as at the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 17 to 18D: the day falls within the weeks for which C is treated as present` a `as at` `the weeks of the absence as at the day` MEANS
        (`regs 17 to 18D: the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a) GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the weeks of the absence as at the day` AT MOST (`regs 17 to 18D: the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)

@ref reg 17(1), reg 18(1), reg 18A(1), reg 18C(1), reg 19(1) (src:183, src:186, src:194, src:204, src:214)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
      `the weeks of the absence as at the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` a `as at` `the weeks of the absence as at the day` MEANS
       a's `regulation 19(1) applies to the absence`
    OR `regs 17 to 18D: the day falls within the weeks for which C is treated as present` a `as at` `the weeks of the absence as at the day`

-- For regulation 16(b): the weeks of an absence that count as weeks of presence: all of them where regulation 19(1)
-- applies, otherwise the weeks of the absence up to the limit of regulations 17 to 18D.
@ref reg 17(1), reg 18(1), reg 18A(1), reg 18C(1), reg 19(1) (src:183, src:186, src:194, src:204, src:214)
GIVEN a IS AN `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` a MEANS
    IF a's `regulation 19(1) applies to the absence`
    THEN a's `the weeks of the absence that fall within the 156 weeks`
    ELSE `regs 17 to 18D: the smaller of two numbers`
             (a's `the weeks of the absence that fall within the 156 weeks`)
             (`regs 17 to 18D: the first weeks of the absence for which C is treated as present` a)

@ref reg 16(b), reg 17(1) (src:173, src:183)
GIVEN as IS A LIST OF `an absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regs 17 to 19: the weeks of all these absences treated as present` as MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` a) as)

§ `Regulations 20, 20A and 21`

-- reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c) where (a) C is
-- resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces; or (b) C is living with a person
-- mentioned in paragraph (a) and is the spouse, civil partner, son, daughter, step-son, step-daughter, father,
-- father-in-law, step-father, mother, mother-in-law or step-mother of that person.
-- src:233 | 20 Serving members of Her Majesty's forces and their family members – further provision
-- src:234 | C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c) where—
-- src:235 | (a) C is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces; or
-- src:236 | (b) C is living with a person mentioned in paragraph (a) and is the spouse, civil partner, son, daughter, step-son, step-daughter, father, father-in-law, step-father, mother, mother-in-law or step-mother of that person.
@ref reg 20 (src:234-236)
GIVEN `C is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is living with a person who is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's relationship to that person` IS A `a relationship to a member of Her Majesty's forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` MEANS
       `C is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces`
    OR (    `C is living with a person who is resident outside Great Britain in the capacity of a member of Her Majesty's forces`
        AND `regs 19(1)(c) and 20(b): the relationship is one that the regulation lists` `C's relationship to that person`)

-- reg 20A: where C is required for the purposes of regulation 16(a) to be present in England and Wales, even though C
-- is absent from England and Wales on a particular day, C is to be treated as though they were present in England and
-- Wales on that day if (a) C's absence on that day is by reason only of the fact that they are temporarily absent from
-- England and Wales, and (b) C is present in Scotland.
-- src:237 | 20A Absence from England and Wales whilst present in Scotland
-- src:238 | Where C is required for the purposes of regulation 16(a) to be present in England and Wales, even though C is absent from England and Wales on a particular day, C is to be treated as though they were present in England and Wales on that day if—
-- src:239 | (a) C’s absence on that day is by reason only of the fact that they are temporarily absent from England and Wales, and
-- src:240 | (b) C is present in Scotland.
@ref reg 20A (src:238-240)
GIVEN `C is required for the purposes of regulation 16(a) to be present in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is absent from England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's absence on that day is by reason only of the fact that C is temporarily absent from England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is present in Scotland on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` MEANS
        `C is required for the purposes of regulation 16(a) to be present in England and Wales`
    AND `C is absent from England and Wales on the day`
    AND `C's absence on that day is by reason only of the fact that C is temporarily absent from England and Wales`
    AND `C is present in Scotland on the day`

-- reg 21: where C is terminally ill and makes a claim for personal independence payment expressly on that ground,
-- regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 82 ("terminally ill")
-- src:241 | 21 Terminal illness
-- src:242 | Where C is terminally ill and makes a claim for personal independence payment expressly on that ground, regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted.
@ref reg 21 (src:242)
GIVEN `C is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C makes a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground that C is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` MEANS
        `C is terminally ill`
    AND `C makes a claim for personal independence payment expressly on the ground that C is terminally ill`

-- The three ways of being treated as present in England and Wales for regulation 16(a) that this module and the next
-- give: regulations 17 to 19, regulation 20A, and the run-on period of regulations 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7).
-- (Regulations 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7) are quoted in pip-part4-special-cases; the locators below are the lines quoted here.)
@ref reg 16(a), reg 17(1), reg 20A, reg 23ZB(2), reg 23ZC(7) (src:171, src:183, src:238)
GIVEN `regulations 17 to 19 treat C as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 20A treats C as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7) treats C as present on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day by one of regulations 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7)` MEANS
       `regulations 17 to 19 treat C as present on the day`
    OR `regulation 20A treats C as present on the day`
    OR `regulation 23ZB(2) or 23ZC(7) treats C as present on the day`
